# Paracord Docker overrides — OPTIONAL. Everything works with NO .env at all.
#
#   docker compose up -d          # zero config; secrets are auto-generated
#
# The server generates and persists a random JWT secret (and self-signed media
# certs) into the /data volume on first run, so there is nothing you must set
# before starting. Copy this file to .env only if you want one of the optional
# overrides below.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored; only this template (.env.example) is tracked.

# Public URL used for CORS and invite links. Auto-detected when unset; set it
# for internet-facing deployments behind a reverse proxy.
# PARACORD_PUBLIC_URL=https://chat.example.com

# --- Built-in TLS (optional) -------------------------------------------------
# The container serves plain HTTP on 8090 by default and expects TLS to be
# terminated at a reverse proxy. To use Paracord's built-in HTTPS instead, set
# this true and mount certificates into /data/certs.
# PARACORD_TLS_ENABLED=true

# --- LiveKit fallback (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Native QUIC/WebTransport media is the default and needs none of this. LiveKit
# is opt-in: start it with `docker compose --profile livekit up -d` and set
# PARACORD_VOICE_NATIVE_MEDIA=false on the paracord service to route through it.
# Both the paracord and livekit services read the secret below; a local dev
# default is used when it is unset. Set a strong random value before exposing
# LiveKit to a network (generate: openssl rand -hex 32).
# PARACORD_LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
